# Auth, Security & RBAC

## JWT Token Strategy
| Token | Storage | TTL |
|---|---|---|
| Access Token | **In-memory only** (Zustand) — lost on refresh, that's intentional | 15 min |
| Refresh Token | httpOnly cookie (backend sets it) — never accessible in JS | 7 days |
| Silent Refresh | On app mount: `POST /auth/refresh` → store new access token before render | — |

**NEVER store access tokens in localStorage or sessionStorage.**

## ProtectedRoute Pattern
```tsx
function ProtectedRoute({ roles }: { roles?: TUserRole[] }) {
  const { user, isAuthenticated } = useAuthStore()
  if (!isAuthenticated) return <Navigate to="/login" replace />
  if (roles && !roles.includes(user.role))
    return <Navigate to="/403" replace />
  return <Outlet />
}
```

## RBAC Role Matrix
| Role | Access |
|---|---|
| `admin` | All routes + `/settings/users` + `/settings/roles` + `/locker` (full) |
| `manager` | `/dashboard`, `/crm/*`, `/locker` (request only), `/notifications` |
| `user` | `/dashboard`, assigned leads/deals/tasks only, `/notifications` |

## Security Checklist (enforce in code review)
- ❌ Never use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` — use DOMPurify for rich text
- ❌ Never log tokens, passwords, or locker values in console (strip in prod via Vite define)
- ❌ Never store sensitive values in URL params or query strings
- ✅ Access token in `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header (not cookie) — defeats CSRF
- ✅ Refresh cookie must be `SameSite=Strict` (backend concern — verify)
- ✅ Validate all redirect params against an allowlist before navigation
- ✅ Run `npm audit` in CI — block deploys on high-severity vulnerabilities
- ✅ CSP headers set via Nginx — restrict script/style sources

## Locker Module Security (critical)
- Encryption/decryption happens **client-side with AES-256** (crypto-js)
- Decrypted values must live **only in local component state** — never in Zustand, React Query cache, or localStorage
- Auto-clear decrypted value on component unmount or route leave
- Never send plaintext credentials over the network
- Locker encrypt/decrypt utilities must have **100% test coverage**
